  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Suh12CKI2p4+Rg02LdV1A6Uy2T0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:05.617Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The mechanism is an Open Zaak notification subscription mirroring each zaak status change as a typed operation, producing an independent case history for municipal audit. It is the same design recorded for the Dimpact group; the two texts differ by an article, which is why claim-level deduplication produced two groups instead of one.\n\nWhat this group adds is the delivery candidate. The single lead is Maykin in Amsterdam, with Open Zaak and Common Ground in its tool column, marked \"1 \u00b7 start here\" \u2014 the only lead carrying either version of this demo at that priority, the other priority-1 entry being marked \"parallel track\" instead.\n\nThat combination matters for sequencing: the demo has a Dutch cohort that wants the outcome (municipal audit independence) and a separate lead positioned as the party to build it with. The Common Ground vocabulary note applies here too, since the same source row records Common Ground alongside Open Zaak.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**1 \u00b7 start here**\n- Maykin (NL Amsterdam) \u2014 not published (first names only) \u00b7 info@maykinmedia.nl \u00b7 https://maykin.nl\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Open Zaak notification subscription mirroring each zaak status change as a typed operation \u2014 an independent case history for municipal audit.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:05.617122Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:05.617127Z"
    }
  },
